    "manuscript/notes/**/*.tex: complete untruncated label search across all supplied LaTeX files; the four relevant labels occur in manuscript/notes/notes_stratonovich_ham_second_moment.tex at lines 190, 745, 767 and 785."
  ],
  "checks": [
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.DampedNormsHomog.GreenMass: L:damped-homogeneous-norms",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "DampedNormsHomog.lean:126-127 states '∀ s, 0 < s → G s univ = ENNReal.ofReal s'. TeX notes_stratonovich_ham_second_moment.tex:825 uses 'G_s(R^d) = s'. The supplied input is exactly that positive-time mass identity, not positivity, regularity or a stronger Green-kernel characterization. Ledger:1019 and claims.yaml:6197-6203 faithfully disclose the arbitrary-family abstraction."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.DampedNormsHomog.N0: E:damped-norm-definitions",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "DampedNormsHomog.lean:131-132 defines the integral without hypotheses; TeX:747 defines the same positive-time mass integral for the wave Green family. Ledger:1020 and claims.yaml:6204-6210 explicitly replace that family by a parameter G and disclose Bochner totalization. Under GreenMass, toReal introduces no infinite-mass discrepancy."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.DampedNormsHomog.N1on: E:damped-norm-definitions",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "DampedNormsHomog.lean:136-137 has unrestricted definition parameters 'a θ S μ' and integrates against L0 restricted to S. TeX:748-750 uses a=alpha0 and the full positive Laplace domain; TeX:789-791 permits domain restriction. Ledger:1021 and claims.yaml:6211-6217 accurately identify the generalized restricted definition, including Gamma normalization."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.DampedNormsHomog.N1tail: E:damped-tail-norms",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "DampedNormsHomog.lean:140 defines 'N1on a 1 (Ioi M) μ', without additional hypotheses. TeX:782 specifies the first norm with 'lambda > M', at damping one. Ledger:1022 and claims.yaml:6218-6224 correctly retain intersection with lambda>0; eventual positive M suffices for the stated tail limit."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.DampedNormsHomog.KS: E:damped-tail-norms",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "DampedNormsHomog.lean:147-148 defines Gamma(a)^(-1) times the subKernel integral on S against L0. TeX:779-780 gives the same kernel for S=(M,infinity), a=alpha0>0. Ledger:1023 and claims.yaml:6225-6231 disclose the generalized domain and divergent diagonal value. In the manuscript parameter range, off-diagonal integrability follows from KS_le, so totalization changes no norm integral."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.DampedNormsHomog.KM: E:damped-tail-norms",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "DampedNormsHomog.lean:152 states 'KS a (Ioi M) r'; TeX:779-780 integrates from M to infinity with a=alpha0. Ledger:1024 and claims.yaml:6232-6238 disclose the positive-Laplace restriction. For M>=0 the formulas coincide, and negative-M extension does not change an M→infinity assertion."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.DampedNormsHomog.N2onOuter: E:damped-tail-norms",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "DampedNormsHomog.lean:155-157 defines the outer integrand without hypotheses. TeX:751-754 supplies the original quadratic form, and TeX:783-784 replaces its power kernel by K_M. Ledger:1025 and claims.yaml:6239-6245 state the same integrand generalized to S; the omitted conjugation is harmless because waveHat is real."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.DampedNormsHomog.N2onIntegrand: E:damped-tail-norms",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "DampedNormsHomog.lean:160-162 defines the triple integrand without hypotheses. TeX:751-754 and 783-784 give precisely its a=alpha0, S=(M,infinity) specialization. Ledger:1026 and claims.yaml:6246-6252 preserve the damping, both wave factors and kernel normalization."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.DampedNormsHomog.N2onSq: E:damped-norm-definitions",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "DampedNormsHomog.lean:165-166 integrates N2onOuter against P2, with no defining hypotheses. TeX:751-754 defines the full squared norm; TeX:789-791 allows temporal-domain restriction. Ledger:1027 and claims.yaml:6253-6259 explicitly describe this restriction rather than equating an arbitrary S with the full norm."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.DampedNormsHomog.N2tailSq: E:damped-tail-norms",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "DampedNormsHomog.lean:170 defines 'N2onSq a 1 (Ioi M) μ'. TeX:783-784 specifies the second norm with K_M replacing the power kernel. Ledger:1028 and claims.yaml:6260-6266 correctly describe its square, with the same positive-Laplace convention already disclosed."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.DampedNormsHomog.N2tail: E:damped-tail-norms",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "DampedNormsHomog.lean:173 defines 'Real.sqrt (N2tailSq a M μ)'. TeX:783-787 uses the unsquared second tail norm. Ledger:1029 and claims.yaml:6267-6273 correctly explain that under H:homog the radicand is proved nonnegative; no negative-radicand totalization is used in the correspondence."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.DampedNormsHomog.smoothed: L:damped-homogeneous-norms",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "DampedNormsHomog.lean:178-179 defines withDensity for 'g : Rd d → NNReal'; measurability and g<=1 are imposed by subsequent theorems. TeX:838-841 describes spectral factors in '[0,1]'. Ledger:940-957,1030 and claims.yaml:6274-6280 explicitly state the adopted multiplier reading and absence of constructed smoothed kernels. TeX:1067-1082 and 1591-1603 support that reading."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.DampedNormsHomog.alpha_pos: no direct label",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "DampedNormsHomog.lean:189-193 assumes 'h : HomogCovariance ...' and concludes '0 < alpha'. TeX:205 assumes '0 < alpha < d, or alpha=d=1'. Ledger:1031 and claims.yaml:6281-6287 match the type. Treating this extraction as an auxiliary rather than a separately labelled manuscript result is appropriate."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.DampedNormsHomog.KS_nonneg: L:damped-homogeneous-norms",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "DampedNormsHomog.lean:196 assumes only 'ha : 0 < a' and concludes nonnegativity for every S,r. TeX:831-833 asserts '0 <= K_M(r)' under H:homog, hence a=alpha0>0. Ledger:1032 and claims.yaml:6288-6294 faithfully state the harmless stronger generality; no extra manuscript hypothesis is required."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.DampedNormsHomog.KS_le: L:damped-homogeneous-norms",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "DampedNormsHomog.lean:204-205 assumes '0 < a' and 'r ≠ 0', proving kernel-integrability and KS<=|r|^(-a). TeX:832-833 gives the same off-diagonal bound for K_M with a=alpha0. Ledger:1033 and claims.yaml:6295-6301 preserve the necessary off-zero restriction and explicitly describe the generalized S."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.DampedNormsHomog.KS_univ: no direct label",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "DampedNormsHomog.lean:216 assumes '0 < a' and 'r ≠ 0' and identifies the unrestricted kernel with |r|^(-a). TeX:821-823 invokes a positive Laplace mixture but does not separately label this unrestricted-kernel identification. Ledger:1034 and claims.yaml:6302-6308 match the type and appropriately avoid claiming a direct labelled identity."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.DampedNormsHomog.tail_tendsto_zero: no direct label",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "DampedNormsHomog.lean:221-222 assumes 'Integrable f L0' and concludes vanishing restricted tail integrals. TeX:831 identifies N1's tail as a tail of a finite integral, but states no general theorem for arbitrary integrable real f. Ledger:1035 and claims.yaml:6309-6315 accurately classify this general auxiliary."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.DampedNormsHomog.KM_tendsto: L:damped-homogeneous-norms",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "DampedNormsHomog.lean:232-233 assumes '0 < a' and 'r ≠ 0' and takes M to atTop. TeX:833 states 'K_M(r) → 0 for r ≠ 0', under a=alpha0>0. Ledger:1036 and claims.yaml:6316-6322 preserve the limit, strictness and exceptional diagonal."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.DampedNormsHomog.weight_scaling: no direct label",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "DampedNormsHomog.lean:242-244 assumes 'SpectralHomogeneous μ alpha', theta>0 and u>0, and gives exponent a+alpha-5. TeX:825-829 instead scales the original norm variables; its weight is defined later at 7683-7688. Ledger:1037 and claims.yaml:6323-6329 correctly present this as a route-only auxiliary. Including d-lambda contributes the extra theta needed for the norm exponent."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.DampedNormsHomog.N2sq_scaling: L:damped-homogeneous-norms",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "DampedNormsHomog.lean:258-260 assumes 'HomogCovariance ...' and '0 < θ', concluding exponent '-(4-alpha-alpha0)'. TeX:768-775 assumes H:homog, theta>0, and states exactly theta^(-beta), beta=4-alpha-alpha0. Ledger:1038 and claims.yaml:6330-6336 match; neither adds Gamma!=0."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.DampedNormsHomog.N1_scaling: L:damped-homogeneous-norms",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "DampedNormsHomog.lean:279-281 assumes spectral homogeneity and theta>0, for any real a, with exponent alpha+a-2. TeX:773 and 795-796 supplies the a=alpha0 specialization and derives that homogeneity. Ledger:1039 and claims.yaml:6337-6343 disclose the broader totalized-integral identity; the wrapper separately proves genuine integrability."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.DampedNormsHomog.N0_eq: L:damped-homogeneous-norms",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "DampedNormsHomog.lean:306-308 assumes 'hG : GreenMass G' and theta>0, proving both integrability and N0=theta^(-2). TeX:769,772 and 825 asserts finiteness and that identity using 'G_s(R^d)=s'. Ledger:1040 and claims.yaml:6344-6350 correctly disclose this exact supplied premise; no stronger Green-family condition is imposed."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.DampedNormsHomog.FKS_integrable: no direct label",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "DampedNormsHomog.lean:326-329 assumes s-finite μ, resolvent-weight integrability, 0<a<1, theta>0 and measurable S. TeX:768 and 795-820 provides the corresponding manuscript range and spectral integrability, but does not introduce FKS. Ledger:1041 and claims.yaml:6351-6357 faithfully identify this restricted subordinated-integrand auxiliary."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.DampedNormsHomog.FKS_apply: no direct label",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "DampedNormsHomog.lean:333-334 has no hypotheses and states the indicator identity. TeX:789-791 discusses restriction but contains no FKS definition or identity. Ledger:1042 and claims.yaml:6358-6364 accurately paraphrase the Lean identity as an auxiliary, not a manuscript proof step."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.DampedNormsHomog.integral_FKS_eq: no direct label",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "DampedNormsHomog.lean:340-342 assumes only 'MeasurableSet S' and proves the identity for every xi,p. TeX:779-784 supplies the kernel construction but no FKS identity. Ledger:1043 and claims.yaml:6365-6371 match the type. The all-p assertion is legitimate as a totalized identity, including the diagonal, rather than a claim of diagonal integrability."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.DampedNormsHomog.inner_FKS_eq: no direct label",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "DampedNormsHomog.lean:361-364 assumes s-finite μ, hR, 'μ {0}=0', theta>0 and lambda>0; it imposes no a-range or S-measurability hypothesis. TeX:796-804 derives the spectral conditions under H:homog, but the lambda-wise weight representation is not a step of this lemma's printed proof. Ledger:1044 and claims.yaml:6372-6378 accurately classify and summarize it."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.DampedNormsHomog.N2onSq_eq: L:damped-homogeneous-norms",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "DampedNormsHomog.lean:393-398 assumes s-finite μ, hR, μ{0}=0, 0<a<1, theta>0 and measurable S, proving two integrability statements and N2onSq=int_S w. TeX:795-820 supplies these spectral conditions and TeX:831-844 concerns the same restricted quadratic forms. The weight equality is an alternative representation, not a literal printed proof step; ledger:988-1001,1045 explicitly says 'Lean route'. This disclosed change is harmless and agrees with claims.yaml:6379-6385."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.DampedNormsHomog.N2onSq_univ: E:damped-norm-definitions",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "DampedNormsHomog.lean:425-426 assumes only a>0 and identifies the unrestricted squared norm, for arbitrary theta,μ. TeX:751-754 uses a=alpha0>0. Ledger:1046 and claims.yaml:6386-6392 match this generalized identity; equality is almost-everywhere in the outer integral, so the diagonal convention creates no discrepancy."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.DampedNormsHomog.N1on_univ: E:damped-norm-definitions",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "DampedNormsHomog.lean:433 states the unrestricted identity with no hypotheses. TeX:748-750 defines precisely that full-domain integral with a=alpha0. Ledger:1047 and claims.yaml:6393-6399 accurately state the definitional identification without claiming integrability for arbitrary parameters."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.DampedNormsHomog.smoothed_sFinite: no direct label",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "DampedNormsHomog.lean:441-442 assumes only '[SFinite μ]' and g:Rd d→NNReal. TeX:193 assumes a Radon spectral measure, hence sufficient finiteness in Euclidean space, but contains no separately stated withDensity instance. Ledger:1048 and claims.yaml:6400-6406 faithfully report the auxiliary and do not add an unstated measurability requirement."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.DampedNormsHomog.integrable_mul_of_le_one: no direct label",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "DampedNormsHomog.lean:447-449 assumes NNReal-valued measurable g, pointwise g<=1 and Integrable f μ. TeX:838-841 uses factors in '[0,1]' but does not state this general integrability lemma. Ledger:1030,1049 and claims.yaml:6407-6413 retain the nonnegative multiplier convention and accurately classify the auxiliary."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.DampedNormsHomog.smoothed_hR: no direct label",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "DampedNormsHomog.lean:458-460 assumes measurable g<=1 and hR, concluding hR for smoothed μ. TeX:800-804 establishes the original spectral integrability and TeX:838 introduces bounded multipliers; it has no separately labelled transfer lemma. Ledger:1050 and claims.yaml:6414-6420 match the exact conditional conclusion."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.DampedNormsHomog.smoothed_zero: no direct label",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "DampedNormsHomog.lean:465-467 assumes only 'μ {0}=0' and concludes the same null singleton for smoothed μ. TeX:796-797 derives μ{0}=0 under H:homog, without stating this transfer. Ledger:1051 and claims.yaml:6421-6427 correctly describe the absolute-continuity auxiliary; neither measurability nor g<=1 is silently added."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.DampedNormsHomog.resolvent_smoothed_le: L:damped-homogeneous-norms",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "DampedNormsHomog.lean:471-473 assumes measurable NNReal g<=1, hR and 'q ≠ 0'. TeX:838-839 removes a '[0,1]' factor from the nonnegative N1 integrand, whose q=theta+lambda is positive by TeX:748-750,769. Ledger:1052 and claims.yaml:6428-6434 preserve the q restriction; the general q!=0 formulation adds no burden to the manuscript application."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.DampedNormsHomog.weight_smoothed_le: L:damped-homogeneous-norms",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "DampedNormsHomog.lean:485-488 assumes measurable g<=1, hR and a,theta,lambda>0. TeX:838-841 compares nonnegative time-integrated forms under H:homog. Ledger:1053 explicitly identifies its different 'comparison at each lambda' route, supported by the nonnegative spectral expression in TeX:7732-7744. This is a harmless disclosed representation change, not a claimed literal reproduction of the printed proof; claims.yaml:6435-6441 matches."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.DampedNormsHomog.N2onSq_smoothed_mono: L:damped-homogeneous-norms",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "DampedNormsHomog.lean:515-521 assumes s-finite μ, hR, μ{0}=0, 0<a<1, theta>0, measurable NNReal g<=1 and measurable S⊆S'. TeX:190-205,795-820 provides the spectral hypotheses, while TeX:789-791,838-844 asserts these smoothing and domain-restriction bounds. Ledger:1054 and claims.yaml:6442-6448 preserve hypotheses and both outer-integrability conclusions. No homogeneity of gμ or Gamma!=0 is required."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.DampedNormsHomog.N1on_smoothed_mono: L:damped-homogeneous-norms",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "DampedNormsHomog.lean:545-551 assumes s-finite μ, hR, a,theta>0, original N1-integrand integrability, measurable NNReal g<=1 and S⊆S'. TeX:805-808 proves the integrability under H:homog and TeX:789-791,838-844 asserts the comparison. Ledger:1055 and claims.yaml:6449-6455 explicitly report the integrability premise; the wrapper discharges it. The more general absence of S-measurability assumptions is accurately stated."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.DampedNormsHomog.homog_spectral_facts: no direct label",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "DampedNormsHomog.lean:583-585 assumes 'HomogCovariance ...' and concludes hR and μ{0}=0. TeX:795-804 derives those facts under H:homog. Ledger:1056 and claims.yaml:6456-6462 correctly treat their Lean bundling as an auxiliary rather than a new labelled manuscript result."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.DampedNormsHomog.N2tail_props: L:damped-homogeneous-norms",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "DampedNormsHomog.lean:595-600 assumes H:homog and arbitrary real M, proving tail integrability, its weight representation and nonnegativity. TeX:832-836 supplies the absolute majorant and nonnegative tail quadratic form under the same hypothesis. Ledger:959-961,988-1001,1057 and claims.yaml:6463-6469 disclose both the positive-Laplace convention and alternative representation. The extension to negative M is harmless for the manuscript tail."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.DampedNormsHomog.N1tail_tendsto: E:damped-tail-norms",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "DampedNormsHomog.lean:613-615 assumes only H:homog and states convergence atTop to zero. TeX:768,782,785-787 states exactly the first tail limit under H:homog. Ledger:1058 and claims.yaml:6470-6476 preserve damping one, the unsquared norm and quantifier order; no nonzero-covariance hypothesis appears."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.DampedNormsHomog.N2tail_tendsto: E:damped-tail-norms",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "DampedNormsHomog.lean:621-624 assumes only H:homog and proves convergence of both N2tailSq and N2tail. TeX:786-787 asserts the unsquared limit and TeX:834-836 proves squared convergence and nonnegativity. Ledger:1059 and claims.yaml:6477-6483 accurately retain both conclusions without an additional Gamma!=0 assumption."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.DampedNormsHomog.damped_homogeneous_norms_paper: L:damped-homogeneous-norms",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "DampedNormsHomog.lean:652-675 assumes 'h : HomogCovariance ...' and 'hG : GreenMass G'; its quantifiers cover every theta>0, every M, and every measurable g<=1 and measurable S⊆S'. TeX:768-791 assumes H:homog and states finiteness, nonnegativity, the three scaling identities, both tails and smoothing/truncation; TeX:825 supplies the exact mass identity. Ledger:1060 and claims.yaml:6484-6490 faithfully summarize this bundle under the explicitly adopted multiplier abstraction. No conclusion, exponent or covariance-zero case is lost."
    },
    {
      "claim": "PARA-DampedNormsHomog",
      "verdict": "PASS_WITH_NOTES",
      "reason": "Ledger:910-1015 correctly discloses the sole supplied mass input, arbitrary G, multiplier interpretation, positive Laplace domain, diagonal totalization, genuine integrability, alternative proof route and unconstructed kernels. Its manuscript anchors agree with the required TeX ranges and uses. Minor W1: ledger:982-986 incorrectly lists Gamma_tempered as used; MaskedSpectralGrowth.lean:315-317 uses only μ_tempered, spectral and scaling to derive spectral homogeneity. This does not alter the theorem's hypotheses or correspondence."
    },
    {
      "claim": "LEDGER-INDEX",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "Ledger:294-298 contains exactly the 42 section declarations: 15 under L:damped-homogeneous-norms, five under E:damped-norm-definitions, nine under E:damped-tail-norms and 13 with no direct label. These agree with rows 1019-1060. The untruncated search across all supplied LaTeX files finds H:homog, E:damped-norm-definitions, L:damped-homogeneous-norms and E:damped-tail-norms at TeX:190,745,767,785, respectively."
    },
    {
      "claim": "COVERAGE-ROWS",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "coverage.yaml:73-103 correctly uses class inputs-supplied, conclusion full, and one supplied GreenMass input, with the multiplier/domain interpretation explicitly noted. The listed claim identifiers resolve in the read claims.yaml module entries. DampedNormsHomog.lean:652-689 supplies the bundle, and ClockCopyHomog.lean:68-86 supplies finiteness/nonnegativity without a separate homogeneity premise. docs/coverage-scope-tex.yaml:1-18 has no entry for this label, consistently with the full-conclusion classification under the disclosed abstraction."
    },
    {
      "claim": "CROSS-REFERENCES",
      "verdict": "PASS_WITH_NOTES",
      "reason": "Ledger:77-87,121-128,249-250,780-784,872,908,2105-2106,2183-2184 and 3156-3160 correctly distinguish the earlier finiteness slice, the whole-result bundle, the supplied mass identity and unconstructed smoothed kernels. Minor W2: the blanket exclusion of 'all limits ... in regularization parameters' at ledger:142 and 3177 is broader than the now-formalized temporal cutoff limits in DampedNormsHomog.lean:613-624. The specific cross-references themselves are accurate."
    }
  ],
  "findings": {
    "fatal": [],
